WEBVTT

00:01:59.189 --> 00:02:00.480
I hurt my arm.

00:02:00.504 --> 00:02:03.558
And, of course, I did what you would do
when you're 22 years old.

00:02:03.582 --> 00:02:05.934
I jumped up and said, "I'm okay, folks."

00:02:06.464 --> 00:02:09.451
And I obviously was not okay.

00:02:09.475 --> 00:02:11.137
AG: (Laughs) Oh, no.

00:02:11.161 --> 00:02:14.064
AB: (Laughs) It was just
so terrible, Adam.

00:02:14.088 --> 00:02:15.770
It was so terrible.

00:02:15.794 --> 00:02:17.786
AG: Arthur tried to shake off the feeling

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:20.106
that falling off the stage was a bad omen.

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.231
He spent the next decade practicing.

00:02:22.255 --> 00:02:24.397
He studied with the best tutors in Europe.

00:02:24.421 --> 00:02:26.949
He got a job at a symphony
in Barcelona, but --

00:02:26.973 --> 00:02:28.147
AB: It was a wreck.

00:02:28.171 --> 00:02:31.408
It was a slow-moving
wreck in my career itself.